{{Quote|And then remember this: the Imperial need for control is so desperate because it is so unnatural. Tyranny requires constant effort. It breaks, it leaks. Authority is brittle. Oppression is the mask of fear. Remember that. And know this, the day will come when all these skirmishes and battles, these moments of defiance, will have flooded the banks of the Empire's authority and then there will be one too many. One single thing will break the siege. Remember this. Try.|Karis Nemik's manifesto|<ref name="Rix">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref>}}
'''Karis Nemik''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] freedom fighter who served as part of a [[Aldhani rebel infiltration team|team]] assigned to [[Aldhani heist|steal]] the quarterly payroll of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Aldhani dam|base]] on [[Aldhani]]. At the time of the mission, the young Nemik was a passionate and idealistic supporter of anti-Imperial causes and was in the stages of drafting a [[The Trail of Political Consciousness|manifesto]] detailing his thoughts on the Empire and its rampant oppression of [[the galaxy]]. Nemik drafted his spoken manifesto the night before the crew's mission, causing him to fall asleep during his watch. As a member of the Aldhani infiltration team under [[Vel Sartha]]'s command, Nemik, a talented astro-navigator, aided in the planning of the robbery and calculated the group's escape trajectory.

Unlike the rest of the Aldhani team, Nemik welcomed the addition of a new recruit, "Clem," the alias of [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], just days before the infiltration. Though the mission was successful at first, the group was discovered while stealing the payroll and engaged in a shootout. Nemik survived the firefight alongside Sartha, Andor, and [[Arvel Skeen]], but he was severely injured when he was crushed by a payload of credits during the escape through the [[Eye of Aldhani]]. Sartha brought Nemik to a doctor on [[Frezno]] sympathetic to the cause, [[Quadpaw]], but Nemik's injuries were too great, and he [[Death|died]] on the operating table after requesting that his manifesto be given to Andor. Andor kept the manifesto and, by [[1 BBY]], had ensured that it was spread across [[the galaxy]] despite the [[Imperial Security Bureau]]'s attempts to silence it.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Surprise from above is never as shocking as one from below.|Karis Nemik|<ref name="Axe">{{Andor|The Axe Forgets}}</ref>}}
Karis Nemik was a [[Gender|male]] [[human]] who was a part of a [[Aldhani rebel infiltration team|team]] of rebels commanded by [[Vel Sartha]]. He joined Sartha, [[Arvel Skeen]], [[Cinta Kaz]], and [[Taramyn Barcona]] on the [[planet]] [[Aldhani]] as part of an [[Aldhani heist|operation]] to rob an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Aldhani Garrison|garrison]] there, hoping to steal the payroll for the entire sector that was located there. When Sartha left camp and returned with a new team member, introduced as "[[Cassian Jeron Andor|Clem]]," the rest of the team was displeased by having to welcome a new face into the fold only days before they intended to go about their plan. Nemik however was more open and welcomed Clem to the team.<ref name="Aldhani" />

During the [[Aldhani heist|Mission on Aldhani]], Nemik was severely injured after being crushed by a payload of [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]]. Andor, Skeen, and Sartha took him to the [[moon]] [[Frezno]] where he was operated on by the four-[[limb]]ed [[Doctor]] [[Quadpaw]]. Despite Quadpaw's attempts, Nemik [[Death|died]] on the operating table. One of his final wishes was to give his [[The Trail of Political Consciousness|manifesto]] to Andor, who took it as he fled, leaving the team.<ref name="The Eye">{{Andor|The Eye}}</ref>

===Legacy===
{{Quote|I'm assuming you've heard it before.''"<br />"''Bits and pieces.''"<br />"''Just keeps spreading, doesn't it?''"<br />"''It's been hard to contain.''"<br />"''Who do you think it is?|Lio Partagaz and Lagret discuss Nemik's manifesto|<ref name="JKE">{{Andor|Jedha, Kyber, Erso}}</ref>}}
Andor eventually took refuge on the planet [[Niamos]],<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref> leaving Nemik's manifesto in a box of his possessions that was hidden above a shower head in a [[Niamos hotel|hotel]] room.<ref name="Daughter">{{Andor|Daughter of Ferrix}}</ref> However, he was soon arrested by the Empire over a minor confrontation and [[Prison|imprisoned]].<ref name="Announcement" /> After [[Narkina 5 prison escape|escaping]] his [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|incarceration]], Andor returned to Niamos and recovered the box from the hotel room while new hotel guests slept there. While checking the box, he opened the manifesto, which begun playing Nemik's recorded content briefly before he closed it again to not disturb the sleeping guests. Learning shortly after that his [[Parent|adoptive mother]], [[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva]], had died,<ref name="Daughter" /> Andor returned to his [[homeworld]] of [[Ferrix]] to attend her [[Maarva's funeral procession|funeral]]. The night he arrived, he stayed in the wreckage of his [[Andor family|family's]] [[Andor family hauler|old hauler]], where he listened to Nemik's manifesto while a thunderstorm raged outside.<ref name="Rix" /> 

The text and audio of the manifesto spread widely throughout the galaxy in the years leading up to the [[Battle of Yavin]]. By [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Andor JKEDate">{{AndorDate|212}}</ref> the Galactic Empire was aware of the manifesto, trying unsuccessfully to prevent its dissemination. In that same year, [[Major]] [[Lio Partagaz]] of the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] listened to the manifesto in the [[ISB conference room]] shortly before his [[Death|suicide]], wondering aloud who might have created it.<ref name="JKE" />

By [[35 ABY]], Nemik's attempt to provide an intellectual basis for the Rebellion would be acknowledged. Historian [[Beaumont Kin]] would describe him as one of the earliest political theorists of the Rebellion in his book ''[[The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''. The work would also feature the only known picture of Nemik, taken during his time on Aldhani.<ref name="RiseAndFall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:KarisNemik-RFGE.png|thumb|200px|right|Karis Nemik was kindly individual, yet radically opposed the Empire.]]
{{Quote|Good to have you, Clem. We'll take all the help we can get.|Karis Nemik|<ref name="Aldhani" />}}
Karis Nemik was a kindly individual who was more receptive of Andor joining the team than the rest of his comrades, whose reactions ranged from discontentment to outrage. Nemik was eager to help Sartha when she explained the plan to their new recruit. Nemik had light skin, [[Color|brown]] hair, and blue eyes. He was right-handed, but favored his left when handling a [[blaster rifle]].<ref name="Axe" /> During his time on Aldhani, he wore a brown coat and red cap.<ref name="Aldhani" />

==Behind the scenes==
Karis Nemik was first pictured in the teaser trailer for the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series, which was released on [[May 26]], [[2022]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|j5UX1Adanis|Andor &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/andor-teaser-trailer}}</ref> He first appeared in "[[Aldhani (episode)|Aldhani]]," the fourth episode of the series,<ref name="Aldhani" /> which aired on [[September 28]], [[2022]].<ref name="Airdate">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-08-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> He was portrayed by [[Alex Lawther]].<ref name="Aldhani" /> Nemik received a card for the [[2023 Topps Star Wars|''Topps Star Wars'']] line released by [[Topps|The Topps Company, Inc.]], where it was stated his homeworld was Aldhani.<ref name="2023 Topps">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars|cardname=Karis Nemik|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/370777/cid/22170389/2023-Topps-Star-Wars-59-Karis-Nemik}}</ref> ''[[Star Wars]]'' lore advisor [[Pablo Hidalgo]] stated this was not the case.<ref name="Pablo Twitter">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1693067125491912721|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2023-08-19|quote=They're not. I doubt they'd call it home either. It sounds like a poor choice of description of a planet they happen to be associated with. {{C|In response to: Hey @pabl0hidalgo @missingwords, in the spirit of recent card game discussion, topps recently dropped a new set but I think these homeworlds don't add up? I guess it's not impossible but I never got a sense all were from aldhani}}|archivedate=20230820012834}}</ref>

Scenes on Aldhani were filmed at the [[Wikipedia:Cruachan Power Station|Cruachan Dam]] and the surrounding [[mountain]]s in the [[Wikipedia:Scottish Highlands|Scottish Highlands]].<ref name="ProductionBrief">{{Getty|url=thewaltdisneystudios/allaccess#!asset/gppr5wpqgb4t74974f8s|text=ANDOR Production Brief V3 FINAL 8-04-22|author=[[Gina McIntyre|McIntyre, Gina]]|date=2022-08-04}}</ref> According to [[Faye Marsay]], Vel Sartha's actress, the scenes were filmed during the middle of the [[Wikipedia:COVID-19 pandemic|COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref name="Real rebellions">{{WebCite|url=https://www.slashfilm.com/1082395/andors-faye-marsay-talks-preparing-to-play-vel-sartha-the-real-rebellions-that-inspired-her-more-exclusive-interview|text=Andor's Faye Marsay Talks Preparing To Play Vel Sartha, The Real Rebellions That Inspired Her & More &#91;Exclusive Interview&#93;|work=Slashfilm.com|author=Anderton, Ethan|date=2022-11-02|archivedate=20250118025616}}</ref> The episode "[[The Eye]]" originally began with [[Jayhold Beehaz]]'s speech. The scene in which Nemik tells Andor he could not sleep was almost not shot due to the bad weather in [[Wikipedia:Scotland|Scotland]]. The crew felt that the foggy and drifty weather made the scene feel weird and dreamy, making the scene not feel like how it felt in the script. The crew decided that they could not put the scene after Beehaz's speech. One crew member had the idea to put the scene at the beginning, and it ended up being swapped with Beehaz's speech.<ref name="Swap scenes">{{WebCite|url=https://www.indiewire.com/2022/12/andor-interview-tony-gilroy-john-gilroy-1234785978/amp|text=‘Andor' Swapped Two Scenes &ndash; and It Sparked a Rebel's Emotional Fire|author=Shachat, Sarah|date=2022-12-02|work=[[Wikipedia:IndieWire|IndieWire]]|archivedate=20221202162056}}</ref>

The astronav unit that Karis uses to navigate the Eye is a Polaroid SX-70 camera decorated with a sextant arc and scope.<ref name="TAF Trivia">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e5-trivia-gallery|text="The Axe Forgets" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref>

